<div class="sec" id="s1">
  <div class="num">01</div>
  <h2>What these tools do</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    An agent is an AI that can act on your computer, not only answer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Claude chat gives you words to work with. Claude Code is a program from
    Anthropic that can read files, change them and run commands: typed
    instructions to your computer. What you ask an AI to do is called a prompt.
  </p>
  <p>
    I use Claude chat to help write a clear request, then give that request to
    Claude Code. You will use those two for the website. Your browser, the app
    you use to visit websites, is where you check the result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delta is a separate app for working with agents and reviewing their changes.
    It is optional here. It has different account requirements and fewer safety
    controls, which I explain before its exercise.
  </p>
  <p>
    You do not have to understand every line the agent writes. You do have to
    check its work. A confident explanation and a working page are different
    things.
  </p>
</div>
